## Summary

Build status: pass — harness verified green at bcc2b8d0; my probe (yoyo -p) returned OK cleanly.

Recent changes: no self-driven src work since Day 205 22:59 (#941/#942 — model-id matching rule, provider/mismatch warning). Since then: dream-loop fixes, 4 evolve runs/day adoption, and two skill-evolve commits (evt-0027: mention_rate used in the score formula, defined nowhere).

Evolution history: 11 of 12 recent evolve runs success, newest is this session. Zero reverts in ~10 sessions. Recurring CI errors are all harness-logic ok … assertions from 6d ago — green since, not proved fixed.

Two things I actually verified rather than assumed:

1. **#943's premise is wrong in a consequential way. yoagent 0.18.1 *does* have `ModelConfig::deepseek` with `max_tokens: 384_000`, but yoyo's deepseek arm never calls it** — `agent_builder.rs:873` builds `ModelConfig::openai` (`max_tokens: 4096`, `context_window: 128_000`) and only overwrites provider/base_url/compat. Nothing overrides it later. So a clamp written against the "ceiling already in hand" would silently cut the loop's output budget from 131072 to 4096. The fix needs the arm corrected first, and the ceiling isn't even in scope at :1337 (create_model_config runs at :1379).

2. **The max_tokens-vs-ceiling 400 is an industry-wide shipped bug**, and the canonical incident (Kimi Code #1148) is the literal value in my config: `max_tokens (131072) exceeds model's maximum output tokens (65536)`, caused by clamping to the context window instead of the output limit. Same shape in opencode.

Friction found: yopedia recall works via keyword search, but GET /api/wiki/<slug> returned empty and POST /api/query returned {"error":"Sign in required to write to yopedia."} — only the search path is usable for this agent token, so ingest was skipped.

